@startuml
title ParaStation/psmpi System Architecture (s000072_b56aad92)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "ParaStation/psmpi Repository" {
  component "Communication Subsystem" as Comm
  component "Progress Manager" as Progress
  component "Connection Manager" as ConnMgr
  component "One-to-Many Scatter" as Scatter
  package "Send Path" {
    component "Send State Machine" as SendSM
  }

  package "Embedded Libfabric Module" {
    component "Verbs Provider" as VerbsProv
  }
}

package "Send Path Data" {
  component "Flow-Control State" as FlowState <<state>>
  component "Packet Buffer" as PacketBuf <<buffer>>
  component "Network Send Descriptor (DD)" as SendDesc <<descriptor>>
  component "Data Descriptor (DD)" as DataDesc <<descriptor>>
  component "Pinned User Data" as PinnedData <<memory>>
  component "Envelope" as Envelope <<control>>
  component "LIBA" as LIBA <<control>>
  component "OD" as OD <<control>>
}

package "Transport Layers" {
  component "OFI/libfabric" as OFI
  component "UCX" as UCX
}

package "CH4 Integration Context" {
  component "CH4 Netmod" as CH4
}

node "Linux Verbs Environment" as VerbsEnv {
  component "libibverbs" as ibv
  component "librdmacm" as rdma
  node "Network Device" as NetDev
}

node "Build & Verification Environment" as BuildEnv {
  component "run-embedded-tests.sh" as RunScript <<script>>
  component "Autotools Workflow\n(autogen.sh, configure, make)" as Autotools <<build>>
  component "hwloc tarball" as Tarball <<artifact>>
  component "hwloc-tree/" as HwlocTree <<directory>>
}

' Communication Subsystem responsibilities and relationships
Comm --> Progress : progress advancement\n+ blocking progress
Comm --> ConnMgr : connection establishment
Comm --> Scatter : one-to-many scatter responsibility
Comm ..> SendSM : send path (design responsibility)
Comm ..> CH4 : integration context

note right of Comm
- Documented design responsibilities:
  - Initialization and finalization
  - Progress advancement and blocking progress
  - Connection establishment
  - One-to-many scatter-style transfer
- Design-note-derived behaviors are documented responsibilities
  (not confirmed public APIs unless separately verified)
end note

' Send Path logic and data interactions
SendSM --> FlowState : check flow status\n(defer or allow)
SendSM --> SendDesc : prepare posted send
SendDesc ..> OFI : post descriptor (when OFI is used)
SendDesc ..> UCX : post descriptor (when UCX is used)

' Direct-access vs packing alternatives
SendDesc ..> PinnedData : direct-access binding\n(pinned user data)
SendSM --> PacketBuf : prepare packet buffer
DataDesc --> PacketBuf : pack payload (no direct access)

' Rendezvous control-field handling
note right of PacketBuf
Rendezvous packet preparation:
- rndv-rts: envelope + LIBA(OD)
- rndv-cts: LIBA + LIBA
- rndv-data: LIBA
Packet buffer carries control info and payload\n(when direct access is not used)
end note

' Transport to Network Device
OFI --> NetDev
UCX --> NetDev

' Embedded Libfabric verbs provider and constraints
OFI ..> VerbsProv : provider integration (optional)
VerbsProv --> ibv
VerbsProv --> rdma

note right of ibv
Minimum version: libibverbs >= 1.1.8
Matching headers required when building from source
end note

note right of rdma
Minimum version: librdmacm >= 1.0.16
Matching headers required when building from source
end note

' Build & Verification: embedded hwloc workflows
RunScript --> Tarball : input tarball
RunScript --> Autotools : executes embedded verification
Autotools --> HwlocTree : build from renamed source dir

note right of BuildEnv
- Preferred verification: run-embedded-tests.sh <tarball>
- Alternative manual workflow:
  - Extract tarball, rename top-level dir to "hwloc-tree/"
  - Run ./autogen.sh, ./configure, make
- Verification is manual and not part of "make check"
- Non-default include/lib locations can be set via
  CFLAGS, LDFLAGS, LD_LIBRARY_PATH
end note

@enduml
